---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE, ACCOUNTS } from '../../config/site';

const title = 'Privacy | AuditYourHouse';
const description = 'What AuditYourHouse collects, why, where it is stored, who sees it, and how to get it corrected or deleted. Plain language, updated October 29, 2026.';
const updated = 'October 29, 2026';
const address = ACCOUNTS.mailingAddress || 'Wakefield, Quebec, Canada';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="container">
    <div class="page-hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Updated {updated}</p>
      <h1>Privacy, plainly</h1>
      <p class="lede">What we collect, why, where it’s kept, who sees it, and how to get it corrected or deleted.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="measure prose">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        AuditYourHouse is operated by Click Shift Marketing, {address}. The person in charge of protecting
        personal information is Dave Bussell, owner: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
        Write to him for any question, request or complaint about your information.
      </p>

      <h2>The planner and calculators</h2>
      <p>
        The home energy planner and the calculators run in your browser. ZIP codes, bills and answers you enter are
        worked out on your device and aren’t sent to us. Your answers stay in your browser: the planner keeps them in
        the part of the page address after the “#” sign, which browsers don’t send to our servers, and our page-view
        analytics don’t receive them. They’re shared only if you copy the link to your plan and send it to someone
        yourself.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions and quote requests</h2>
      <p>
        If you send us a question or a heat pump quote request through a form on this site, or by email, we use your
        details to answer you, and for no other purpose. We answer ourselves; we don’t pass your request to a
        contractor or an auditor unless you ask us to, we don’t sell contact lists, and no company pays us for your
        details.
      </p>
      <p>
        Forms are handled by Netlify, the company that hosts this site. It stores what you submit in the United
        States and emails it to us, and we keep it only as long as we need to deal with your request. If you email
        us, we have your email address; we use it to reply.
      </p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        We use Google Analytics and Microsoft Clarity to see which pages are useful and where people get stuck. They
        set cookies and record how pages are used; Clarity can replay a visit, with what you type in our forms hidden.
        Neither receives your planner answers. You can block them with your browser’s privacy settings or an ad
        blocker; the site works the same.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies we set ourselves</h2>
      <p>
        One: a cookie that remembers that you chose this site over our Canadian one, so we stop suggesting the
        switch. It holds no personal information and expires after a year.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        Some gear guides link to Amazon through the Amazon Associates program. If you buy something after following
        one of those links we may earn a commission; Amazon’s own privacy notice covers what happens on its site.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what we hold about you, correct it, get a copy, or have it deleted, whatever state you live in;
        we answer every request the same way. Email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
        Because we are based in Canada, the information you send us is handled there and, through Netlify, in the
        United States.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>Emails and form submissions are kept as long as needed to deal with them, then deleted.</p>

      <p class="small">
        If we change how we handle personal information, we’ll update this page and the date at the top.
        Questions: <a href={`mailto:${SITE.contactEmail}`}>{SITE.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .prose p { margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 22px; margin: 28px 0 8px; }
  .prose h2:first-child { margin-top: 0; }
  .prose { padding-bottom: 56px; }
</style>
